{"_v":1,"id":"matilda-the-musical-west-end-2021","bd":{"positive":25,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Quentin Letts","o":"Daily Mail","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.dailymail.co.uk/tvshowbiz/reviews/article-2065957/Matilda-musical-review-A-beasty-baddie-stonking-songs--it-all.html","d":"2011-11-24","q":"Matilda is a fabulous family fizzer."},{"cn":"Patrick Marmion","o":"Daily Mail","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.dailymail.co.uk/tv/article-15340469/Marmalade-magic-Paddington-Musical-scale-cuteness-PATRICK-MARMION-reviews-opening-night-Londons-Savoy-Theatre.html"},{"cn":"Henry Hitchings","o":"Evening Standard","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.thisislondon.co.uk/theatre/review-24014294-matilda-the-musical-cambridge-theatre---review.do","d":"2011-11-25","q":"This generous, big-hearted piece is already being spoken of as one of the best new British musicals in years."},{"cn":"Tim Bano","o":"Evening Standard","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/paddington-the-musical-savoy-theatre-review-b1260368.html"},{"cn":"Lyn Gardner","o":"The Guardian","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.guardian.co.uk/stage/2011/nov/25/matilda-review","d":"2011-11-25","q":"It's an evening of unadulterated bliss."},{"cn":"Emma Brockes","o":"The Guardian","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2011/nov/27/matilda-the-musical-roald-dahl","d":"2011-11-27","q":"You'd be a nitwit to miss this hit show."},{"cn":"Charles Spencer","o":"The Telegraph","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/matilda-cambridge-theatre-review/","d":"2011-11-25","q":"It is the best new British musical since Billy Elliot."},{"cn":"Jessica Green","o":"Daily Mail","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.dailymail.co.uk/lifestyle/article-11286507/Matilda-Musicals-rising-star-Alisha-Weir.html","d":"2022-10-06"},{"cn":"Clive Davis","o":"The Times (UK)","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.com/culture/theatre-dance/article/paddington-the-musical-review-this-singing-bear-will-capture-your-heart-kr397ksdm"},{"cn":"Tim Walker","o":"The Telegraph","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/theatre/theatre-reviews/8915418/Matilda-the-Musical-Cambridge-Theatre-Seven-magazine-review.html","d":"2011-11-25","q":"But the tremendous heart and intelligence of the piece remains undimmed."},{"cn":"Peter Brown","o":"London Theatre","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/matilda-the-musical-review","d":"2011-11-24","q":"Matilda the Musical is nevertheless hugely enjoyable and cracking Christmas fun."},{"cn":"Fiona Mountford","o":"The i","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://inews.co.uk/culture/arts/paddington-musical-will-conquer-world-4074185","d":"2025-12-01"},{"cn":"Alice Saville","o":"The Independent","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/paddington-the-musical-west-end-b2874351.html"},{"cn":"Mark Shenton","o":"The Stage","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/2018/matilda-musical-review-curve-leicester/","d":"2018-03-16","q":"\"Warchus’ peerless production...is spectacularly staged. It feels both intimate and larger-than-life as we see the world through the unique prism of the older-than-her-years Matilda, a voracious reader and loner who is neglected by her parents..."},{"cn":"Andy Plaice","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/west-end-theatre/news/11-2011/matilda-the-musical_6129.html/","d":"2018-03-16","q":"Powerful, funny and beautifully musical, it reminds us who we are, and who we might be."},{"cn":"Sarah Crompton","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/paddington-the-musical-west-end-review-a-paw-fect-stage-adaptation_1704856/"},{"cn":"Lisa Martland","o":"The Stage","s":89,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/review.php/34349/matilda-the-musical","q":"They have created a fresh and intelligent family entertainment that brings joy to both adults and children (crucially never patronising the latter)."},{"cn":"Sam Marlowe","o":"The Stage","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/paddington-the-musical-review-savoy-theatre-london-michael-bond-tom-fletcher-jessica-swale"},{"cn":"Andrzej Lukowski","o":"Time Out London","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/news/review-paddington-the-musical-at-the-savoy-theatre-113025","q":"Smart, quirky and sublimely good fun. A moving and subtle spectacle which will have kids in stitches and adults in tears. It is g…Read more →"},{"cn":"Sarah Hemming","o":"Financial Times","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.ft.com/content/b34f9d9c-16b0-11e1-be1d-00144feabdc0","q":"But it’s still dark, daring and a lot of fun."},{"cn":"Michael Coveney","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":73,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://www.whatsonstage.com/reviews/theatre/london/E8831322212171/Matilda.html","q":"But there are a few bumps in the adaptation by Dennis Kelly, and Tim Minchin's songs are deficient in nothing except melody"},{"cn":"Danai G Miliaraki","o":"London Box Office","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.londonboxoffice.co.uk/news/post/matilda-musical-review","d":"2024-09-26","q":"Matilda The Musical, produced by the Royal Shakespeare Company, is an explosion of energy, colours, creativity and talent."},{"cn":"Julie Carpenter","o":"The Express","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"http://www.express.co.uk/posts/view/285905/Theatre-review-Matilda-The-Musical-Cambridge-Theatre-London","d":"2011-11-25","q":"Gloriously over the top it’s an irresistible and ingenious mix of fun, fizz, cruelty, incredible choreography and above all warmth which means we root for the kids from the start."},{"cn":"Lizzie Loveridge","o":"One-Minute Critic","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://theatrevibe.co.uk/2011/11/22/review-matilda-the-musical-cambridge-theatre-2011/","q":"The RSC may have as big a hit with Matilda as they did with Les Miserables back in 1985."},{"cn":"Carole Woddis","o":"The Arts Desk","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://theartsdesk.com/theatre/matilda-musical-cambridge-theatre","d":"2011-11-25","q":"This Matilda is a cunning combination of gross cartoon, pitch-perfect professionalism and endearing feel-good factor."},{"cn":"Nicky & Rosie Chambers","o":"London Box Office","s":85,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.londonboxoffice.co.uk/news/post/matilda-double-review","d":"2015-09-18","q":"We would definitely recommend it to adults and children over 8 and especially to all Roald Dahl lovers out there."}],"au":{"score":90,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"ss":{"s":90,"c":1268},"mz":{"s":83,"c":4002,"sr":4.2},"sp":{"s":94,"c":3637,"sr":4.69},"lb":{"s":94,"c":1469,"sr":4.7},"ltd":{"s":93,"c":5085,"sr":4.7}}},"hi":"https://images.ctfassets.net/6pezt69ih962/5mepwgNH8Kcz5sqrZqC6Qg/21bd74ff35dce76a0155e1019aeff6cf/1440x580.jpg?fm=webp&q=90"}